{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "canvas-operation-pipeline",
  "title": "How one canvas edit call runs",
  "description": "Pipeline that every Codecaine Canvas edit tool runs, from tool definition to result (canvas/src/session/tools/operations/operation-tool.ts).\n\n**Reading order**: top row left to right: Tool definition (OperationSpec → defineOperationTool → Tool descriptor), then Runtime validation (Schema validation, with its own runtime validation error end). The `execute` wire enters runOperation, whose 13 stages run top to bottom in four columns, left to right: Run the edit (1–3), Reconcile the draft (4–6), Guard checks (7–10, diamonds), Commit and report (11–13). Each stage links to the next with `next`.\n\n**Results** (bottom row, Call results): red wires go to ERROR (spec.validate, Section auto-grow, Held-move, Broken-wire, Section rule checks), gray wires go to NO-OP (spec.apply, Zero-delta check), and the green `APPLIED headline` wire runs from operationPerception to APPLIED. ERROR and NO-OP both lead to \"Draft unchanged, no event\"; an edge-target NO-OP also carries the edge's numbered route. Only the commit column changes the board. Result node names carry the result line formats.\n\n**Color key**: blue nodes = tool definition; violet = pipeline stage; orange diamonds = checks; green = commit path / APPLIED; red = error; gray = no-op / unchanged. Stickies hold per-stage details and the known waypoint-replay gap (in Reconcile the draft).",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
